# 📋 Documentation Terminology Quick Reference

> **One concept. One preferred name.**

---

# Purpose

Provide a concise reference for the preferred terminology used throughout the Engineering Documentation System (EDS).

Use this document while writing documentation to maintain consistency across repositories.

---

# Core Documentation Terms

| Preferred Term | Use For |
|----------------|---------|
| Standard | Defines engineering rules and requirements. |
| Reference | Explains the reasoning, philosophy, and evolution behind a Standard. |
| Quick Reference | Concise, task-oriented guide for everyday use. |
| Procedure | Step-by-step operational instructions. |
| Template | Starting point for creating consistent documents. |
| Roadmap | Future direction and planned work. |
| WWAN | *Where We Are Now* — current operational state. |

---

# AFK Terms

| Preferred Term | Use For |
|----------------|---------|
| Journey | Guided learning experience. |
| Learning Path | Recommended sequence for learning. |
| Playbook | Repeatable engineering workflow. |
| Methodology | Reusable engineering approach. |
| Discovery | Structured investigation before modification. |

---

# EKS Terms

| Preferred Term | Use For |
|----------------|---------|
| Knowledge Package | Reusable engineering knowledge. |
| Architecture Finding | Validated architectural observation. |
| Organizational Knowledge | Knowledge preserved beyond individuals. |

---

# Lifecycle Terms

| Preferred Term | Meaning |
|----------------|---------|
| Planning | Proposed work. |
| In Progress | Active development. |
| Under Review | Awaiting review. |
| Accepted | Approved baseline ready for adoption. |
| Official | Mature, validated engineering guidance. |
| Superseded | Replaced by a newer document. |
| Archived | Historical reference only. |

---

# Business vs Engineering

| Business Term | Preferred Engineering Term |
|---------------|----------------------------|
| Feature | Capability |
| Screen | Page / View |
| Customer | User |
| Issue | Defect / Bug |

---

# Legacy Terminology

| Legacy | Preferred |
|---------|-----------|
| Canonical | Standard |
| Official Standard | Standard |
| Companion Guide | Quick Reference |

---

# Quick Rules

✅ Use the preferred terminology consistently.

✅ Prefer clarity over jargon.

✅ Use one name for one concept.

✅ Update terminology through the Terminology Standard before adopting new vocabulary.

